<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle $105-$106/dressed,thin-private.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle $105-$106/dressed,thin-private.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nebraska feedlot cattle traded in light volume at $105.00-$106.00 per cwt on a dressed basis, steady with Wednesday's brisk sales, market sources said.</p>
<p>About 500 steers and heifers that will likely grade select and choice were sold, which brought the week to date estimate to 103,500, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;The showlist is sold out and business is to the point where basically there is nothing left,&quot; a cattle source said.</p>
<p>This week's showlist had been estimated earlier in the week at 93,000 head.</p>
<p>((Bob Janis 312-983-7347))</p>
